 {:seon.task/name "forks-live-in-one-place"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: .gitmodules points the submodules into experiment directories (reference-code/jolt -> ~/src/seon-jolt/jolt, chez -> e14/chez-share, datahike and konserve -> libs/, persistent-sorted-set -> e4/pss-a, and others), so the ~100 GB of old experiments (l1, l2, pf1, r4, r5, fx1, proto, scratch, perf, l3, x1, e*) cannot be removed without breaking `git submodule update` and clones of next/. Correct (owner 2026-10-23: next becomes the root folder, self-contained; the module store is the home): .gitmodules url ./.git/modules/reference-code/<name> (a relative URL resolves against the superproject when it has no remote, and a clone, and a clone of a clone, resolve into their own .git/modules), after every source branch and copy is a local head or tag in that module (step B, done 2026-10-23); the measurements, the stray branches and the steps are notes/self-contained-plan-2026-10-23.md (steps B and C); then `git submodule sync` in the main tree only; a fresh `git clone --recurse-submodules` of next/ builds (bin/build seon) and bin/check is green. Then the owner deletes the experiment directories (the owner's act; list them with sizes). Also the move plan's precondition (forks pushable from one place)."
